				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for FileSystem and Git IPC standardization\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from ec2fef2 to 086cbf4 to integrate the `JsonValueHelpers` utility into the FileSystem and Git IPC handler namespaces.\n\n**Mountain:** Apply the centralized argument extraction helpers (`arg_string`, `arg_u64`, `arg_bool_true`) to the `FileMkdir`, `FileCloseFd`, and `HandleExec` handlers. This eliminates verbose `Arguments.get(...).and_then(...).unwrap_or(...)` chains, aligning these specific modules with the recent refactoring of the WindServiceHandlers tree.\n\nThis ensures uniform type safety and default value handling across the entire Mountain backend IPC surface, covering both the general command handlers and the specific file/extension system operations.",
			"SHA": "78ffe4cacf4b119b479f8e10ad7e56d25ee59f60"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T10:42:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for standardized Wind service argument handling\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 8c65e3c to ec2fef2 to integrate the refactoring of IPC argument extraction in Mountain.\n\n**Mountain:** Introduce the `JsonValueHelpers` utility module to provide type-safe, default-aware extraction functions (`arg_string`, `arg_u64`, `arg_bool`, etc.). Replace fragmented `Arguments.get(n).and_then(...).unwrap_or(...)` patterns across 40+ IPC handler modules with calls to these centralized helpers.\n\nThis change affects the entire `WindServiceHandlers` tree, covering Cocoon, Git, Terminal, UI, and NativeHost namespaces. The `mod.rs` exports and the main `mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatcher are updated to utilize the new utilities, ensuring consistent default value handling, reducing boilerplate, and improving type safety across the Mountain backend's IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "656f32c6ffe1632608db17eb92e42f0cce84ef2a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T10:33:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate Cocoon forwarding logic via macro\n\nEliminate the fragmented `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers` directory structure containing repetitive boilerplate for forwarding IPC commands to the Cocoon extension host. Introduce a centralized `forward_to_cocoon` macro and `cocoon_payload` helper in `mod.rs` to unify payload serialization and gRPC invocation.\n\nThis refactoring consolidates the handling logic for SCM, Debug, Tasks, and Authentication namespaces within the main IPC dispatcher. The new macro standardizes argument normalization and manages the connection lifecycle, significantly reducing code duplication while preserving the functional bridge to the VS Code runtime.",
			"SHA": "f62307d656582ee216c55a5bed8ebb0fb298ec14"
		}
